      <abstract>The Congregational Church at Quality Hill was organized in 1810 in Lenox, New York.
        The first settled pastor of the church was Rev. Ira M. Olds. By 1860, the church was known
        as the First Congregational Church. The church variously, and likely simultaneously,
        associated with Congregational and Presbyterian denominations throughout its history. The
        church likely dissolved in 1906. This collection contains administrative church records,
        society records, and important membership records and includes church and society meeting
        minutes, financial records, correspondence, and Sunday school attendance records.</abstract>
