    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>The Congregational Church at Quality Hill was organized in 1810 and was the first church to
        be formed in Lenox, New York. Lenox itself was formed in 1809 from land which had been a
        part of the neighboring town of Sullivan. The first settled pastor of the church was Rev.
        Ira M. Olds. The Lenox Anti-Slavery Society was formed at the church. By 1860, the church
        was known as the First Congregational Church. The church seems to have associated with both
        Congregational and Presbyterian denominations. By the end of the church's existence, it
        seems likely that the church primarily associated with the Presbyterians. The date of the
        church's dissolution is likely 1906 based on Hall's Index of American Presbyterian
        Congregations.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>This collection contains administrative church records, society records, and important
        membership records for the First Congregational Church in Lenox, New York. The collection
        includes meeting minutes, membership records, financial records, a year's Sunday school
        attendance records, and letters to Congregational and Presbyterian missionary
        organizations.</p>
    </scopecontent>
    <arrangement>
      <head>Arrangement</head>
      <p>Materials in this collection have been arranged into chronological order by start date.</p>
    </arrangement>
